<ManagementPackFragment SchemaVersion="2.0" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
<!--
%%
Description:
  A CLASS and DISCOVERY and MONITOR and PERFORMANCE COLLECTION RULE which share a SINGLE PowerShell data source across ALL discovered instances using COOKDOWN
  One scheduled PowerShell script runs per agent, returns one propertybag PER INSTANCE, and every monitor and rule for every instance is fed from that single execution
  The example discovers one instance per subfolder found under a base folder, and collects the number of files in each instance folder as a numeric metric
  CompanyID - is a short abbreviation for your company with NO SPACES OR SPECIAL CHARACTERS ALLOWED
  AppName - is a short name for your app with NO SPACES OR SPECIAL CHARACTERS ALLOWED
  UniqueID - We need a Unique ID to reuse the fragment within the same MP.  Use a shortened descriptive name with NO SPACES OR SPECIAL CHARACTERS ALLOWED such as "QueueDepth"
  BaseFolderPath - the folder scanned by BOTH the discovery and the shared collection script.  Each subfolder becomes one discovered instance.  Example: C:\Demo\Queues
  IntervalSeconds - how often the SHARED collection script runs.  This value is used by the monitor AND the collection rule and they MUST match for cookdown
  ObjectName - you can make this up, it is the Performance Object name the collected data is mapped to
  CounterName - you can make this up, it is the Performance Counter name the collected data is mapped to
  Threshold - the numeric value which, when EXCEEDED, drives the monitor unhealthy
  Samples - the number of CONSECUTIVE breaching samples required before the monitor changes state

  HOW COOKDOWN WORKS IN THIS FRAGMENT:
    The shared data source (##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Collection.DS) contains a Scheduler and a PowerShell propertybag probe.
    Its configuration contains ONLY values that are identical for every instance on an agent (IntervalSeconds, SyncTime, BaseFolderPath, TimeoutSeconds).
    Nothing instance specific (InstanceName, Threshold, Samples, ObjectName, CounterName) is ever passed into the data source.
    The script emits one propertybag per instance, each carrying the instance key (InstanceName) and the numeric metric (Value).
    Each workflow then filters DOWNSTREAM of the shared data source for its own instance using an expression filter on Property[@Name='InstanceName'].
    Because the expanded module chain (Scheduler + PowerShell probe) and its configuration are byte for byte identical for every workflow,
    the agent instantiates that chain ONCE and multicasts the output to every monitor and every rule that needs it.

  COOKDOWN BOUNDARIES - READ THIS BEFORE YOU MODIFY THE FRAGMENT:
    1. Cookdown happens INSIDE A SINGLE HEALTH SERVICE (one agent, one management server, or one gateway).  It NEVER shares a script execution between different agents.
       Fifty agents each running this MP means fifty script executions per interval - one per agent - no matter how many instances each agent hosts.
    2. All of the sharing workflows must be loaded in the SAME module host / execution context on that agent.  Isolation="Any" is used here so the agent is free to place them together.
       Changing Isolation, or adding a RunAs profile to only some of the workflows, puts those workflows in a different execution context and they will NOT share.
    3. The data source configuration must resolve to the SAME literal string for every workflow.  $Target$ references are resolved BEFORE the comparison, so a
       $Target/Property[...]$ value that differs per instance in the data source configuration silently defeats cookdown.  Keep all of those downstream.
    4. Overrides that change DATA SOURCE configuration split the sharing group.  In this fragment those are IntervalSeconds, SyncTime, BaseFolderPath and TimeoutSeconds.
       Override IntervalSeconds for three instances out of twenty and you get TWO script executions per interval on that agent, not one.
    5. Overrides that change only DOWNSTREAM configuration are safe and do NOT break cookdown.  In this fragment those are Threshold and Samples on the monitor.
    6. Disabling the monitor (or the rule) for some instances is safe - those workflows simply stop, the rest keep sharing.  Disabling every sharing workflow stops the script entirely.
    7. If you change the monitor interval you MUST change the rule interval to the identical value, otherwise the monitor and the rule each run their own copy of the script.

Version: 1.0
LastModified: 11-Sep-2026
%%

In this fragment you need to replace:
  ##CompanyID##
  ##AppName##
  ##UniqueID##
  ##BaseFolderPath##
  ##IntervalSeconds##
  ##ObjectName##
  ##CounterName##
  ##Threshold##
  ##Samples##

This fragment depends on references:
  RequiredReference: Alias="System", ID="System.Library"
  RequiredReference: Alias="SC", ID="Microsoft.SystemCenter.Library"
  RequiredReference: Alias="Windows", ID="Microsoft.Windows.Library"
  RequiredReference: Alias="Health", ID="System.Health.Library"
  RequiredReference: Alias="Perf", ID="System.Performance.Library"
  RequiredReference: Alias="MSDL", ID="Microsoft.SystemCenter.DataWarehouse.Library"

@@Author=FragmentLibrary Contributor@@
-->
  <TypeDefinitions>
    <EntityTypes>
      <ClassTypes>
        <ClassType ID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Instance.Class" Base="Windows!Microsoft.Windows.LocalApplication" Accessibility="Public" Abstract="false" Hosted="true" Singleton="false">
          <Property ID="InstanceName" Type="string" Key="true" CaseSensitive="false" MaxLength="256" MinLength="0" Required="true" />
          <Property ID="FolderPath" Type="string" Key="false" MaxLength="512" />
          <!-- We choose Microsoft.Windows.LocalApplication as our generic base class.  It is hosted by Microsoft.Windows.Computer, which gives every instance a stable host -->
          <!-- InstanceName is the KEY property.  The key plus the host computer form the instance identity, so the key must be stable across discovery cycles -->
        </ClassType>
      </ClassTypes>
    </EntityTypes>
    <ModuleTypes>
      <DataSourceModuleType ID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Instance.Discovery.DS" Accessibility="Internal" Batching="false">
        <Configuration>
          <xsd:element minOccurs="1" name="IntervalSeconds" type="xsd:integer" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" />
          <xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="SyncTime" type="xsd:string" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" />
          <xsd:element minOccurs="1" name="BaseFolderPath" type="xsd:string" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" />
          <xsd:element minOccurs="1" name="DebugLogging" type="xsd:boolean" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" />
          <xsd:element minOccurs="1" name="TimeoutSeconds" type="xsd:integer" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" />
        </Configuration>
        <OverrideableParameters>
          <OverrideableParameter ID="IntervalSeconds" Selector="$Config/IntervalSeconds$" ParameterType="int" />
          <OverrideableParameter ID="SyncTime" Selector="$Config/SyncTime$" ParameterType="string" />
          <OverrideableParameter ID="BaseFolderPath" Selector="$Config/BaseFolderPath$" ParameterType="string" />
          <OverrideableParameter ID="DebugLogging" Selector="$Config/DebugLogging$" ParameterType="bool" />
          <OverrideableParameter ID="TimeoutSeconds" Selector="$Config/TimeoutSeconds$" ParameterType="int" />
        </OverrideableParameters>
        <ModuleImplementation Isolation="Any">
          <Composite>
            <MemberModules>
              <DataSource ID="DS" TypeID="Windows!Microsoft.Windows.TimedPowerShell.DiscoveryProvider">
                <IntervalSeconds>$Config/IntervalSeconds$</IntervalSeconds>
                <SyncTime>$Config/SyncTime$</SyncTime>
                <ScriptName>##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Instance.Discovery.DS.ps1</ScriptName>
                <ScriptBody>
#=================================================================================
#  Discovers one class instance for each subfolder found under a base folder
#  This is the discovery half of a cookdown example - the collection half returns
#  one propertybag per instance discovered here, keyed on the same InstanceName
#
#  Author:
#  v1.0
#=================================================================================
param($SourceId,$ManagedEntityId,$ComputerName,$MGName,$BaseFolderPath,$DebugLogging)


# Manual Testing section - put stuff here for manually testing script - typically parameters:
#=================================================================================
# $SourceId = '{00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000}'
# $ManagedEntityId = '{00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000}'
# $ComputerName = "computername.domain.com"
# $MGName = "MGNAME"
# $BaseFolderPath = "C:\Demo\Queues"
# $DebugLogging = "false"
#=================================================================================


# Constants section - modify stuff here:
#=================================================================================
# Assign script name variable for use in event logging.
# ScriptName should be the same as the ID of the module that the script is contained in
$ScriptName = "##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Instance.Discovery.DS.ps1"
$EventID = "4801"
#=================================================================================


# Starting Script section - All scripts get this
#=================================================================================
# Gather the start time of the script
$StartTime = Get-Date
#Set variable to be used in logging events
$whoami = whoami
# Load MOMScript API
$momapi = New-Object -comObject MOM.ScriptAPI
#Log script event that we are starting task
$momapi.LogScriptEvent($ScriptName,$EventID,0,"`n Script is starting. `n Running as ($whoami). `n Management Group: ($MGName). `n BaseFolderPath: ($BaseFolderPath).")
#=================================================================================


# Discovery Script section - Discovery scripts get this
#=================================================================================
# Load SCOM Discovery module
$DiscoveryData = $momapi.CreateDiscoveryData(0, $SourceId, $ManagedEntityId)
#=================================================================================


# Begin MAIN script section
#=================================================================================
# Enumerate the instance folders.  A read failure here must NOT submit an empty snapshot,
# because an empty snapshot would delete every previously discovered instance on this agent.
$InstanceFolders = $null
$ReadFailed = $false
TRY
{
  IF (Test-Path -LiteralPath $BaseFolderPath -PathType Container)
  {
    $InstanceFolders = @(Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath $BaseFolderPath -Force -ErrorAction Stop | Where-Object {$_.PSIsContainer -eq $true})
  }
  ELSE
  {
    # The base folder genuinely does not exist.  This is a valid "nothing is installed here" result and we submit an empty snapshot on purpose.
    $InstanceFolders = @()
    $momapi.LogScriptEvent($ScriptName,$EventID,0,"`n BaseFolderPath ($BaseFolderPath) does not exist. Submitting an empty discovery snapshot - no instances on this computer.")
  }
}
CATCH
{
  $ReadFailed = $true
  $momapi.LogScriptEvent($ScriptName,$EventID,1,"`n FATAL ERROR: Unable to enumerate ($BaseFolderPath). `n Error: $($_.Exception.Message) `n NOT submitting discovery data so existing instances are preserved.")
}

IF ($ReadFailed -eq $true)
{
  # Exit WITHOUT returning $DiscoveryData.  Returning an empty snapshot after a read failure would remove healthy objects and close their alerts incorrectly.
  $EndTime = Get-Date
  $ScriptTime = ($EndTime - $StartTime).TotalSeconds
  $momapi.LogScriptEvent($ScriptName,$EventID,1,"`n Script Completed WITHOUT submitting discovery data. `n Script Runtime: ($ScriptTime) seconds.")
  EXIT
}

$InstanceCount = 0
FOREACH ($Folder in $InstanceFolders)
{
  [string]$InstanceName = $Folder.Name
  [string]$FolderPath = $Folder.FullName

  $instance = $DiscoveryData.CreateClassInstance("$MPElement[Name='##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Instance.Class']$")
  $instance.AddProperty("$MPElement[Name='Windows!Microsoft.Windows.Computer']/PrincipalName$", $ComputerName)
  $instance.AddProperty("$MPElement[Name='##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Instance.Class']/InstanceName$", $InstanceName)
  $instance.AddProperty("$MPElement[Name='##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Instance.Class']/FolderPath$", $FolderPath)
  $instance.AddProperty("$MPElement[Name='System!System.Entity']/DisplayName$", $InstanceName)
  $DiscoveryData.AddInstance($instance)
  $InstanceCount++

  IF ($DebugLogging.ToUpper() -eq "TRUE")
  {
    $momapi.LogScriptEvent($ScriptName,$EventID,0,"`n DEBUG: Discovered instance ($InstanceName) at ($FolderPath).")
  }
}

$momapi.LogScriptEvent($ScriptName,$EventID,0,"`n Discovery script is returning ($InstanceCount) instances from ($BaseFolderPath).")

# Return Discovery Items Normally
$DiscoveryData
# Return Discovery Bag to the command line for testing (does not work from ISE)
# $momapi.Return($DiscoveryData)
#=================================================================================
# End MAIN script section


# End of script section
#=================================================================================
#Log an event for script ending and total execution time.
$EndTime = Get-Date
$ScriptTime = ($EndTime - $StartTime).TotalSeconds
$momapi.LogScriptEvent($ScriptName,$EventID,0,"`n Script Completed. `n Script Runtime: ($ScriptTime) seconds.")
#=================================================================================
# End of script
                </ScriptBody>
                <Parameters>
                  <Parameter>
                    <Name>SourceId</Name>
                    <Value>$MPElement$</Value>
                  </Parameter>
                  <Parameter>
                    <Name>ManagedEntityId</Name>
                    <Value>$Target/Id$</Value>
                  </Parameter>
                  <Parameter>
                    <Name>ComputerName</Name>
                    <Value>$Target/Host/Property[Type="Windows!Microsoft.Windows.Computer"]/PrincipalName$</Value>
                  </Parameter>
                  <Parameter>
                    <Name>MGName</Name>
                    <Value>$Target/ManagementGroup/Name$</Value>
                  </Parameter>
                  <Parameter>
                    <Name>BaseFolderPath</Name>
                    <Value>$Config/BaseFolderPath$</Value>
                  </Parameter>
                  <Parameter>
                    <Name>DebugLogging</Name>
                    <Value>$Config/DebugLogging$</Value>
                  </Parameter>
                </Parameters>
                <TimeoutSeconds>$Config/TimeoutSeconds$</TimeoutSeconds>
              </DataSource>
            </MemberModules>
            <Composition>
              <Node ID="DS" />
            </Composition>
          </Composite>
        </ModuleImplementation>
        <OutputType>System!System.Discovery.Data</OutputType>
      </DataSourceModuleType>
      <DataSourceModuleType ID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Collection.DS" Accessibility="Internal" Batching="false">
        <!-- THIS IS THE SHARED (COOKED DOWN) DATA SOURCE.  Every monitor and every collection rule for every instance uses THIS module with THIS configuration. -->
        <!-- DO NOT add instance specific configuration here.  Anything added here that differs per instance will break cookdown and multiply the script executions. -->
        <Configuration>
          <xsd:element minOccurs="1" name="IntervalSeconds" type="xsd:integer" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" />
          <xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="SyncTime" type="xsd:string" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" />
          <xsd:element minOccurs="1" name="BaseFolderPath" type="xsd:string" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" />
          <xsd:element minOccurs="1" name="TimeoutSeconds" type="xsd:integer" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" />
        </Configuration>
        <OverrideableParameters>
          <!-- Every parameter exposed here changes the SHARED data source configuration.  Overriding any of them for a SUBSET of instances creates a second sharing group. -->
          <OverrideableParameter ID="IntervalSeconds" Selector="$Config/IntervalSeconds$" ParameterType="int" />
          <OverrideableParameter ID="SyncTime" Selector="$Config/SyncTime$" ParameterType="string" />
          <OverrideableParameter ID="BaseFolderPath" Selector="$Config/BaseFolderPath$" ParameterType="string" />
          <OverrideableParameter ID="TimeoutSeconds" Selector="$Config/TimeoutSeconds$" ParameterType="int" />
        </OverrideableParameters>
        <ModuleImplementation Isolation="Any">
          <Composite>
            <MemberModules>
              <DataSource ID="Scheduler" TypeID="System!System.Scheduler">
                <Scheduler>
                  <SimpleReccuringSchedule>
                    <Interval Unit="Seconds">$Config/IntervalSeconds$</Interval>
                    <SyncTime>$Config/SyncTime$</SyncTime>
                  </SimpleReccuringSchedule>
                  <ExcludeDates />
                </Scheduler>
              </DataSource>
              <ProbeAction ID="PA" TypeID="Windows!Microsoft.Windows.PowerShellPropertyBagTriggerOnlyProbe">
                <ScriptName>##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Collection.DS.ps1</ScriptName>
                <ScriptBody>
#=================================================================================
#  SHARED (cooked down) collection script
#  Runs ONCE per agent per interval and returns ONE propertybag PER INSTANCE
#  Each propertybag carries:
#    InstanceName - the stable instance key, identical to the discovery key property
#    Value        - the numeric metric for that instance
#  Downstream expression filters in each monitor and each rule pick out their own instance
#
#  Author:
#  v1.0
#=================================================================================
param([string]$BaseFolderPath)


# Manual Testing section - put stuff here for manually testing script - typically parameters:
#=================================================================================
# [string]$BaseFolderPath = "C:\Demo\Queues"
#=================================================================================


# Constants section - modify stuff here:
#=================================================================================
# Assign script name variable for use in event logging.
$ScriptName = "##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Collection.DS.ps1"
$EventID = "4802"
#=================================================================================


# Starting Script section - All scripts get this
#=================================================================================
# Gather the start time of the script
$StartTime = Get-Date
#Set variable to be used in logging events
$whoami = whoami
# Load MOMScript API
$momapi = New-Object -comObject MOM.ScriptAPI
#=================================================================================


# Begin MAIN script section
#=================================================================================
# NOTE: we deliberately do NOT create the propertybag here.  One bag is created PER INSTANCE inside the loop below.

$InstanceFolders = @()
TRY
{
  IF (Test-Path -LiteralPath $BaseFolderPath -PathType Container)
  {
    $InstanceFolders = @(Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath $BaseFolderPath -Force -ErrorAction Stop | Where-Object {$_.PSIsContainer -eq $true})
  }
  ELSE
  {
    $momapi.LogScriptEvent($ScriptName,$EventID,1,"`n ERROR: BaseFolderPath ($BaseFolderPath) does not exist. Returning no propertybags - every monitor fed by this script keeps its previous state.")
  }
}
CATCH
{
  $momapi.LogScriptEvent($ScriptName,$EventID,1,"`n FATAL ERROR: Unable to enumerate ($BaseFolderPath). `n Error: $($_.Exception.Message) `n Returning no propertybags - every monitor fed by this script keeps its previous state.")
}

# We never emit a fake numeric value on failure.  A bag with a made up value would silently drive every monitor healthy.
# Emitting nothing leaves each monitor in its previous state and leaves a gap in the performance data, which is honest and visible.

[int]$BagCount = 0
[string]$Summary = ""
FOREACH ($Folder in $InstanceFolders)
{
  [string]$InstanceName = $Folder.Name
  TRY
  {
    # This is the metric.  Replace this block with whatever numeric value your application exposes for one instance.
    [double]$Value = @(Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath $Folder.FullName -Force -ErrorAction Stop | Where-Object {$_.PSIsContainer -eq $false}).Count
  }
  CATCH
  {
    $momapi.LogScriptEvent($ScriptName,$EventID,1,"`n ERROR: Unable to read instance ($InstanceName) at ($($Folder.FullName)). `n Error: $($_.Exception.Message) `n Skipping this instance for this cycle.")
    CONTINUE
  }

  # One propertybag per instance.  CreatePropertyBag must be called inside the loop or every instance overwrites the last.
  $bag = $momapi.CreatePropertyBag()
  $bag.AddValue('InstanceName',$InstanceName)
  $bag.AddValue('Value',$Value)
  $bag
  $BagCount++
  $Summary = $Summary + "`n  ($InstanceName) = ($Value)"
}

$momapi.LogScriptEvent($ScriptName,$EventID,0,"`n Shared collection script returned ($BagCount) propertybags from ($BaseFolderPath). `n Running as ($whoami). $Summary")
#=================================================================================
# End MAIN script section


# End of script section
#=================================================================================
#Log an event for script ending and total execution time.
$EndTime = Get-Date
$ScriptTime = ($EndTime - $StartTime).TotalSeconds
$momapi.LogScriptEvent($ScriptName,$EventID,0,"`n Script Completed. `n Script Runtime: ($ScriptTime) seconds.")
#=================================================================================
# End of script
                </ScriptBody>
                <Parameters>
                  <Parameter>
                    <Name>BaseFolderPath</Name>
                    <Value>$Config/BaseFolderPath$</Value>
                  </Parameter>
                </Parameters>
                <TimeoutSeconds>$Config/TimeoutSeconds$</TimeoutSeconds>
              </ProbeAction>
            </MemberModules>
            <Composition>
              <Node ID="PA">
                <Node ID="Scheduler" />
              </Node>
            </Composition>
          </Composite>
        </ModuleImplementation>
        <OutputType>System!System.PropertyBagData</OutputType>
      </DataSourceModuleType>
      <ConditionDetectionModuleType ID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.InstanceFilterAndPerfMapper.CD" Accessibility="Internal" Batching="false" Stateful="false" PassThrough="false">
        <!-- A Rule may only contain a SINGLE ConditionDetection element, so the per instance filter and the performance mapper are combined into one composite condition detection -->
        <Configuration>
          <xsd:element minOccurs="1" name="InstanceName" type="xsd:string" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" />
          <xsd:element minOccurs="1" name="ObjectName" type="xsd:string" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" />
          <xsd:element minOccurs="1" name="CounterName" type="xsd:string" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" />
        </Configuration>
        <ModuleImplementation Isolation="Any">
          <Composite>
            <MemberModules>
              <ConditionDetection ID="InstanceFilter" TypeID="System!System.ExpressionFilter">
                <Expression>
                  <SimpleExpression>
                    <ValueExpression>
                      <XPathQuery Type="String">Property[@Name='InstanceName']</XPathQuery>
                    </ValueExpression>
                    <Operator>Equal</Operator>
                    <ValueExpression>
                      <Value Type="String">$Config/InstanceName$</Value>
                    </ValueExpression>
                  </SimpleExpression>
                </Expression>
              </ConditionDetection>
              <ConditionDetection ID="PerfMapper" TypeID="Perf!System.Performance.DataGenericMapper">
                <ObjectName>$Config/ObjectName$</ObjectName>
                <CounterName>$Config/CounterName$</CounterName>
                <InstanceName>$Config/InstanceName$</InstanceName>
                <Value>$Data/Property[@Name='Value']$</Value>
              </ConditionDetection>
            </MemberModules>
            <Composition>
              <Node ID="PerfMapper">
                <Node ID="InstanceFilter" />
              </Node>
            </Composition>
          </Composite>
        </ModuleImplementation>
        <OutputType>Perf!System.Performance.Data</OutputType>
        <InputTypes>
          <InputType>System!System.PropertyBagData</InputType>
        </InputTypes>
      </ConditionDetectionModuleType>
    </ModuleTypes>
    <MonitorTypes>
      <UnitMonitorType ID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Threshold.MonitorType" Accessibility="Internal">
        <MonitorTypeStates>
          <MonitorTypeState ID="ThresholdNotBreached" NoDetection="false" />
          <MonitorTypeState ID="ThresholdBreached" NoDetection="false" />
        </MonitorTypeStates>
        <Configuration>
          <!-- The first four elements are passed STRAIGHT THROUGH to the shared data source and must stay identical across every instance for cookdown -->
          <xsd:element minOccurs="1" name="IntervalSeconds" type="xsd:integer" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" />
          <xsd:element minOccurs="0" name="SyncTime" type="xsd:string" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" />
          <xsd:element minOccurs="1" name="BaseFolderPath" type="xsd:string" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" />
          <xsd:element minOccurs="1" name="TimeoutSeconds" type="xsd:integer" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" />
          <!-- These three are used DOWNSTREAM of the shared data source only.  Overriding them is cookdown safe -->
          <xsd:element minOccurs="1" name="InstanceName" type="xsd:string" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" />
          <xsd:element minOccurs="1" name="Threshold" type="xsd:double" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" />
          <xsd:element minOccurs="1" name="Samples" type="xsd:integer" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" />
        </Configuration>
        <OverrideableParameters>
          <!-- COOKDOWN BREAKING when overridden for a subset of instances -->
          <OverrideableParameter ID="IntervalSeconds" Selector="$Config/IntervalSeconds$" ParameterType="int" />
          <OverrideableParameter ID="SyncTime" Selector="$Config/SyncTime$" ParameterType="string" />
          <OverrideableParameter ID="BaseFolderPath" Selector="$Config/BaseFolderPath$" ParameterType="string" />
          <OverrideableParameter ID="TimeoutSeconds" Selector="$Config/TimeoutSeconds$" ParameterType="int" />
          <!-- COOKDOWN SAFE - these only affect modules downstream of the shared data source -->
          <OverrideableParameter ID="Threshold" Selector="$Config/Threshold$" ParameterType="double" />
          <OverrideableParameter ID="Samples" Selector="$Config/Samples$" ParameterType="int" />
        </OverrideableParameters>
        <MonitorImplementation>
          <MemberModules>
            <DataSource ID="DS" TypeID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Collection.DS">
              <IntervalSeconds>$Config/IntervalSeconds$</IntervalSeconds>
              <SyncTime>$Config/SyncTime$</SyncTime>
              <BaseFolderPath>$Config/BaseFolderPath$</BaseFolderPath>
              <TimeoutSeconds>$Config/TimeoutSeconds$</TimeoutSeconds>
            </DataSource>
            <ConditionDetection ID="ThresholdNotBreachedFilter" TypeID="System!System.ExpressionFilter">
              <Expression>
                <And>
                  <Expression>
                    <SimpleExpression>
                      <ValueExpression>
                        <XPathQuery Type="String">Property[@Name='InstanceName']</XPathQuery>
                      </ValueExpression>
                      <Operator>Equal</Operator>
                      <ValueExpression>
                        <Value Type="String">$Config/InstanceName$</Value>
                      </ValueExpression>
                    </SimpleExpression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression>
                    <SimpleExpression>
                      <ValueExpression>
                        <XPathQuery Type="Double">Property[@Name='Value']</XPathQuery>
                      </ValueExpression>
                      <Operator>LessEqual</Operator>
                      <ValueExpression>
                        <Value Type="Double">$Config/Threshold$</Value>
                      </ValueExpression>
                    </SimpleExpression>
                  </Expression>
                </And>
              </Expression>
            </ConditionDetection>
            <ConditionDetection ID="ThresholdBreachedFilter" TypeID="System!System.ExpressionFilter">
              <Expression>
                <And>
                  <Expression>
                    <SimpleExpression>
                      <ValueExpression>
                        <XPathQuery Type="String">Property[@Name='InstanceName']</XPathQuery>
                      </ValueExpression>
                      <Operator>Equal</Operator>
                      <ValueExpression>
                        <Value Type="String">$Config/InstanceName$</Value>
                      </ValueExpression>
                    </SimpleExpression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression>
                    <SimpleExpression>
                      <ValueExpression>
                        <XPathQuery Type="Double">Property[@Name='Value']</XPathQuery>
                      </ValueExpression>
                      <Operator>Greater</Operator>
                      <ValueExpression>
                        <Value Type="Double">$Config/Threshold$</Value>
                      </ValueExpression>
                    </SimpleExpression>
                  </Expression>
                </And>
              </Expression>
              <SuppressionSettings>
                <MatchCount>$Config/Samples$</MatchCount>
              </SuppressionSettings>
            </ConditionDetection>
            <!-- Value LessEqual Threshold and Value Greater Threshold are exhaustive and mutually exclusive for every numeric value, so no sample is ever unhandled and no two states can both match -->
          </MemberModules>
          <RegularDetections>
            <RegularDetection MonitorTypeStateID="ThresholdNotBreached">
              <Node ID="ThresholdNotBreachedFilter">
                <Node ID="DS" />
              </Node>
            </RegularDetection>
            <RegularDetection MonitorTypeStateID="ThresholdBreached">
              <Node ID="ThresholdBreachedFilter">
                <Node ID="DS" />
              </Node>
            </RegularDetection>
          </RegularDetections>
          <!-- There is deliberately no OnDemandDetection.  An on demand (recalculate health) detection would have to run the script outside the shared schedule and would not be cooked down -->
        </MonitorImplementation>
      </UnitMonitorType>
    </MonitorTypes>
  </TypeDefinitions>
  <Monitoring>
    <Discoveries>
      <Discovery ID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Instance.Discovery" Target="Windows!Microsoft.Windows.Server.OperatingSystem" Enabled="true" ConfirmDelivery="false" Remotable="true" Priority="Normal">
      <!-- We choose Microsoft.Windows.Server.OperatingSystem as the preferred target class to ensure this will run on all Windows Servers, but will not create duplicates on clusters -->
        <Category>Discovery</Category>
        <DiscoveryTypes>
          <DiscoveryClass TypeID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Instance.Class">
            <Property PropertyID="InstanceName" />
            <Property PropertyID="FolderPath" />
          </DiscoveryClass>
        </DiscoveryTypes>
        <DataSource ID="DS" TypeID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Instance.Discovery.DS">
          <IntervalSeconds>14400</IntervalSeconds>  <!-- 4 hours.  A new instance folder is monitored within one discovery cycle, and a removed folder is deleted from SCOM on the next cycle -->
          <SyncTime></SyncTime>
          <BaseFolderPath>##BaseFolderPath##</BaseFolderPath>
          <DebugLogging>false</DebugLogging>
          <TimeoutSeconds>120</TimeoutSeconds>
        </DataSource>
      </Discovery>
    </Discoveries>
    <Rules>
      <Rule ID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Collection.Rule" Enabled="true" Target="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Instance.Class" ConfirmDelivery="false" Remotable="true" Priority="Normal" DiscardLevel="100">
        <Category>PerformanceCollection</Category>
        <DataSources>
          <DataSource ID="DS" TypeID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Collection.DS">
            <!-- THESE FOUR VALUES MUST BE IDENTICAL TO THE MONITOR CONFIGURATION BELOW OR THE RULE AND THE MONITOR WILL EACH RUN THEIR OWN COPY OF THE SCRIPT -->
            <IntervalSeconds>##IntervalSeconds##</IntervalSeconds>
            <SyncTime></SyncTime>
            <BaseFolderPath>##BaseFolderPath##</BaseFolderPath>
            <TimeoutSeconds>120</TimeoutSeconds>
          </DataSource>
        </DataSources>
        <ConditionDetection ID="CD" TypeID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.InstanceFilterAndPerfMapper.CD">
          <InstanceName>$Target/Property[Type="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Instance.Class"]/InstanceName$</InstanceName>
          <ObjectName>##ObjectName##</ObjectName>
          <CounterName>##CounterName##</CounterName>
        </ConditionDetection>
        <WriteActions>
          <WriteAction ID="WriteToDB" TypeID="SC!Microsoft.SystemCenter.CollectPerformanceData" />  <!-- Collect this data to the Operations Database -->
          <WriteAction ID="WriteToDW" TypeID="MSDL!Microsoft.SystemCenter.DataWarehouse.PublishPerformanceData" />  <!-- Collect this data to the Data Warehouse Database -->
        </WriteActions>
      </Rule>
    </Rules>
    <Monitors>
      <UnitMonitor ID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Threshold.Monitor" Accessibility="Public" Enabled="true" Target="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Instance.Class" ParentMonitorID="Health!System.Health.PerformanceState" Remotable="true" Priority="Normal" TypeID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Threshold.MonitorType" ConfirmDelivery="false">
        <Category>PerformanceHealth</Category>
        <AlertSettings AlertMessage="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Threshold.Monitor.AlertMessage">
          <AlertOnState>Warning</AlertOnState>  <!-- Warning or Error should match OperationalStates below -->
          <AutoResolve>true</AutoResolve>
          <AlertPriority>Normal</AlertPriority>
          <AlertSeverity>MatchMonitorHealth</AlertSeverity>  <!-- Common options for AlertSeverity are MatchMonitorHealth, Information, Warning, Error -->
          <AlertParameters>
            <AlertParameter1>$Data/Context/Property[@Name='InstanceName']$</AlertParameter1>
            <AlertParameter2>$Data/Context/Property[@Name='Value']$</AlertParameter2>
            <AlertParameter3>$Target/Host/Property[Type="Windows!Microsoft.Windows.Computer"]/PrincipalName$</AlertParameter3>
          </AlertParameters>
        </AlertSettings>
        <OperationalStates>
          <OperationalState ID="ThresholdNotBreached" MonitorTypeStateID="ThresholdNotBreached" HealthState="Success" />
          <OperationalState ID="ThresholdBreached" MonitorTypeStateID="ThresholdBreached" HealthState="Warning" />  <!-- HealthState = Warning or Error -->
        </OperationalStates>
        <Configuration>
          <!-- THESE FOUR VALUES MUST BE IDENTICAL TO THE RULE CONFIGURATION ABOVE OR THE RULE AND THE MONITOR WILL EACH RUN THEIR OWN COPY OF THE SCRIPT -->
          <IntervalSeconds>##IntervalSeconds##</IntervalSeconds>
          <SyncTime></SyncTime>
          <BaseFolderPath>##BaseFolderPath##</BaseFolderPath>
          <TimeoutSeconds>120</TimeoutSeconds>
          <!-- Instance specific configuration lives here, DOWNSTREAM of the shared data source -->
          <InstanceName>$Target/Property[Type="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Instance.Class"]/InstanceName$</InstanceName>
          <Threshold>##Threshold##</Threshold>  <!-- Value GREATER than this is unhealthy.  Value LESS THAN OR EQUAL TO this is healthy -->
          <Samples>##Samples##</Samples>  <!-- Number of consecutive breaching samples required before the monitor changes state -->
        </Configuration>
      </UnitMonitor>
    </Monitors>
  </Monitoring>
  <Presentation>
    <StringResources>
      <StringResource ID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Threshold.Monitor.AlertMessage" />
    </StringResources>
  </Presentation>
  <LanguagePacks>
    <LanguagePack ID="ENU" IsDefault="true">
      <DisplayStrings>
        <!-- Classes -->
        <DisplayString ElementID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Instance.Class">
          <Name>##CompanyID## ##AppName## ##UniqueID## Instance</Name>
          <Description />
        </DisplayString>
        <DisplayString ElementID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Instance.Class" SubElementID="InstanceName">
          <Name>Instance Name</Name>
        </DisplayString>
        <DisplayString ElementID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Instance.Class" SubElementID="FolderPath">
          <Name>Folder Path</Name>
        </DisplayString>
        <!-- Discoveries -->
        <DisplayString ElementID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Instance.Discovery">
          <Name>##CompanyID## ##AppName## ##UniqueID## Instance Discovery</Name>
          <Description />
        </DisplayString>
        <!-- Rules -->
        <DisplayString ElementID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Collection.Rule">
          <Name>##CompanyID## ##AppName## ##UniqueID## Shared Script Performance Collection Rule</Name>
          <Description />
        </DisplayString>
        <!-- Monitors -->
        <DisplayString ElementID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Threshold.Monitor">
          <Name>##CompanyID## ##AppName## ##UniqueID## Threshold Monitor</Name>
          <Description />
        </DisplayString>
        <DisplayString ElementID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Threshold.Monitor" SubElementID="ThresholdNotBreached">
          <Name>Threshold Not Breached</Name>
        </DisplayString>
        <DisplayString ElementID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Threshold.Monitor" SubElementID="ThresholdBreached">
          <Name>Threshold Breached</Name>
        </DisplayString>
        <DisplayString ElementID="##CompanyID##.##AppName##.##UniqueID##.Threshold.Monitor.AlertMessage">
          <Name>##CompanyID## ##AppName## ##UniqueID## has breached a threshold</Name>
          <Description>The shared collection script reported a value above the configured threshold.

Instance: {0}
Value: {1}
Computer: {2}</Description>
        </DisplayString>
      </DisplayStrings>
    </LanguagePack>
  </LanguagePacks>
</ManagementPackFragment>
